messages:
Sam: Heads-up — after yesterday's kernel-autopick roll we saw a 12% tail-latency bump on 8xA100 jobs, focusing on TP+PP config. nvprof/Nsight traces look noisy. Anyone else seeing this?
Maya: saw it in the nightly. throughput is fine but p99 token latency jumps intermittently. suspect all-reduce tailing. :thinking:
Eric: can you paste the job id or trace? I want to check whether it's comm skew or microbatch placement.
Sam: job: rwd-infer/2026-03-15/ks-roll-42. Uploaded an nvtx-labeled nsight capture: /tmp/nsight/ks42-capture.qdrep. Profiling-bot: automatic-summary attached: "allreduce_tail_stddev=0.67x, comm_compute_overlap=0.72, kvcache_prefetch_blocks=4"
Carla: quick thought — kernel chooser now prefers the new fused-attn kernel for batch sizes > 16, could change compute shape and reduce overlap. Also we recently changed KV cache prefetch window from 2->4.
Maya: interesting — increased prefetch can introduce more cross-rank syncs if we eagerly materialize KV across TP boundaries. Can someone run the nsight capture with `REDWOOD_RUNTIME_TRACE=nsight:full` and `RW_KERNEL_PICK=legacy` to compare?
Eric: I'll run a short repro with microbatch=2, seq=2048, tp=2 pp=2. Command: `scripts/run_repro.sh --job ks42 --tp 2 --pp 2 --mb 2 --seq 2048 --trace nsight`
profiling-bot: nsight capture queued: /tmp/nsight/ks42-compare.qdrep (expected ~6m). Will post link when done.
Sam: also add the custom timers we instrumented last month — `batch_schedule_ms`, `kv_prefetch_ms`, `allreduce_wait_ms`. that helped earlier to separate scheduling vs comm stalls.
Carla: here is the small snippet to emit timers in runtime (paste):
```
// on main loop
auto t0 = now();
schedule_batch();
auto t1 = now();
emit_timer("batch_schedule_ms", t1-t0);
kv_prefetch();
auto t2 = now();
emit_timer("kv_prefetch_ms", t2-t1);
allreduce_step();
auto t3 = now();
emit_timer("allreduce_wait_ms", t3-t2);
```
Maya: perfect. If allreduce_wait_ms spikes correlate with p99, then it's comm tail. If kv_prefetch_ms spikes first then prefetch ordering is the culprit.
Eric: nsight compare finished. Early look: fused-attn path increases small kernel count but individual kernels are heavier; allreduce shows tail instances aligning with a few ranks doing extra prefetch before the reduce. Heatmap: we have a diagonal band where rank 3/7 consistently lags.
Sam: rank skew — could be non-deterministic placement of data shards. Any recent changes to scatter/shard logic in the sharding allocator?
Carla: allocator PR changed deterministic seed for slab allocation in v0.12.7 — might cause different memory layout and affect kernel launch timing. Reverting that in a canary might help.
Maya: let's run two experiments: (A) force kernel picker to legacy and prefetch=2, (B) keep fused pick but add `KV_PREFETCH_ASYNC=1` so it doesn't block on materialization. Compare p99 and allreduce_wait_ms distributions.
Sam: I kicked off both. Can we also add a short nvprof run to sample `cudaLaunch` vs `cudaMemcpy` timing and export a waterfall? Command for repro: `NVPROF_CMD="nvprof --print-gpu-trace --csv -o nvprof.csv" scripts/run_repro.sh ...`
profiling-bot: experiment logs: /ci/artifacts/ks42/compare-v1 (A) and (B). Initial numbers: (A) p99 drop ~9%, allreduce_wait_ms stddev down 0.4x. (B) p99 drop ~6%, kv_prefetch_ms mean down 25% but occasional spikes remain.
Eric: looks like prefetch async helps reduce mean but fused kernel plus allocator skew still leaves some ranks tailing. We should add a rank-heartbeat histogram emitted at microsecond resolution to find which op precedes the rank lag.
Carla: I'll add heartbeat and a lightweight per-rank sampler (1%) and push to ks42-canary. If it reproduces, plan: revert allocator non-determinism and then reintroduce with padding to align launch times.
Sam: thanks. Action items: Eric to add rank heartbeat + run expanded nsight on canary; Carla to push allocator revert PR for canary; Maya to collate timer histograms and nvprof waterfalls and open a ticket with attached traces. :thumbsup:
